id: pm-field-key-recovery
title: Name the rejected custom field in extension-field recovery
description: Unknown extension-field refusals populate recovery.provided_fields with the declared legal keys and omit the rejected key from the normalized CLI detail. Agents cannot identify which field to repair without another inspection.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-07T18:37:37.192Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T19:53:36.705Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-07T19:53:35.936Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-07T19:53:35.936Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "SDK refusals separate the rejected input from the legal field domain; normalized CLI JSON and human recovery expose the actual rejected key; registered extension field writes and reserved core-field recovery remain compatible; focused and full-source exact coverage, docstring and static gates pass"
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: Unknown extension-field errors identify the rejected key in field/provided_fields while sorted legal registered keys remain in recovery next steps. Inlined the single-use core-field expression and documented the recovery semantics.
expected_result: "Agents receive rejected caller input separately from legal choices, with stable typed and human refusals and byte-identical item/history storage."
actual_result: "All four linked field/recovery suites passed 267 cases after a failing regression control. Isolated installed npm/npx and Bun/bunx CLI refusals reported provided_fields=[missing], exposed legal choices, exited 2 and left item/history bytes unchanged. Full source suite passed 9,897 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
